# Prettier formats only the TypeScript bindings in guest-js/ and the
# TypeScript, JavaScript and JSON configuration files at the root. The rest is
# out of scope: Rust has rustfmt, example/ is a separate application with its
# own lockfile, Cargo.lock and package-lock.json belong to their package
# managers, permissions/ is generated by the Tauri build, vendor/ is a
# checksummed snapshot, and Markdown would reflow prose.
#
# .prettierrc.json holds the settings that change the fewest existing lines:
# no semicolons, single quotes, arrow parameters without parentheses, and lines
# up to 200 columns, because the bindings keep each call on one line.
/*
!/guest-js/
!/.prettierrc.json
!/eslint.config.js
!/knip.config.ts
!/package.json
!/release.json
!/tsconfig.json
